WEBVTT

00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:09.440
Mattermost is a secure
collaboration hub trusted by

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:12.875
cyber defense and critical
infrastructure organizations.

00:00:12.875 --> 00:00:16.075
It offers on premise and
private cloud deployment for

00:00:16.075 --> 00:00:17.915
strict data control.

00:00:17.915 --> 00:00:20.715
Unlike other cloud based
collaboration tools,

00:00:20.715 --> 00:00:23.435
which may go down
during a cyber attack,

00:00:23.435 --> 00:00:25.675
Mattermost can run out of band,

00:00:25.675 --> 00:00:28.830
ensuring defenders stay
operational and isolated from

00:00:28.830 --> 00:00:30.570
compromised infrastructure.

00:00:30.670 --> 00:00:34.750
It integrates with the Microsoft
stack including Azure and EntraID,

00:00:34.750 --> 00:00:36.830
as well as upcoming
integrations with critical

00:00:36.830 --> 00:00:40.045
security tools like Sentinel,
Defender, and Intune.

00:00:40.045 --> 00:00:42.445
Whether you're replacing
siloed chat apps,

00:00:42.445 --> 00:00:45.485
inefficient email chains,
or other legacy tools,

00:00:45.485 --> 00:00:49.065
Mattermost is the command
center for secure operations.

00:00:53.005 --> 00:00:56.080
From mitigating cybersecurity
incidents to streamlining

00:00:56.080 --> 00:00:57.740
operational coordination,

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:00.240
Mattermost increases the
effectiveness of mission

00:01:00.240 --> 00:01:01.740
critical workflows.

00:01:03.680 --> 00:01:05.040
In this example scenario,

00:01:05.040 --> 00:01:08.365
a security operations center
uses Mattermost to accelerate

00:01:08.365 --> 00:01:12.205
incident response out of band.

00:01:12.205 --> 00:01:15.245
They use a shared channel with
their managed security services

00:01:15.245 --> 00:01:17.005
provider for monitoring alerts.

00:01:17.005 --> 00:01:19.790
By securely connecting
two Mattermost instances,

00:01:19.790 --> 00:01:22.990
both organizations can
collaborate in real time.

00:01:22.990 --> 00:01:26.730
A new alert from the SIM system
posts to the monitoring channel.

00:01:29.390 --> 00:01:32.350
The team lead sends an urgent
message notifying impacted

00:01:32.350 --> 00:01:35.530
personnel who then acknowledge
they've read the message.

00:01:42.165 --> 00:01:45.445
A Mattermost Playbook is
then initiated to execute incident

00:01:45.445 --> 00:01:47.025
response procedures.

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:51.770
The playbook creates a
dedicated channel with a

00:01:51.770 --> 00:01:55.210
standardized checklist, auto invites
key stakeholders, and guides each

00:01:55.210 --> 00:01:57.470
step of the incident response.

00:01:58.050 --> 00:02:00.890
Throughout the incident,
team members mark task progress,

00:02:00.890 --> 00:02:04.450
post status updates, and share
intel in real time.

00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:07.490
Playbooks can be templated and
customized to fit any workflow.

00:02:10.135 --> 00:02:13.735
Slash Commands and Webhooks
trigger actions such as initiating

00:02:13.735 --> 00:02:16.775
a multi party briefing call
directly from the operational channel.

00:02:16.775 --> 00:02:19.975
This pulls the team into a
real time collaboration space.

00:02:20.855 --> 00:02:23.515
Live transcription ensures
team members remain informed.

00:02:26.790 --> 00:02:30.230
After the call concludes,
chat logs, call transcripts,

00:02:30.230 --> 00:02:33.190
and audio recordings are
preserved in the call thread,

00:02:33.190 --> 00:02:37.030
providing critical mission documentation
for an after action review.

00:02:37.030 --> 00:02:39.845
Mattermost Copilot,
your AI assistant,

00:02:39.845 --> 00:02:42.885
extracts key takeaways with
automated call summaries,

00:02:42.885 --> 00:02:46.485
delivering concise insights
when every moment counts.

00:02:46.485 --> 00:02:49.525
Users can refine summaries with
their preferred model and share

00:02:49.525 --> 00:02:51.200
them in the call thread.

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:55.040
With full control over AI
model selection, data access,

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:56.560
and user permissions,

00:02:56.560 --> 00:03:00.400
Mattermost ensures access to
AI support in compliance with

00:03:00.400 --> 00:03:02.060
security standards.

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:07.735
From coordinating remediation
to tracking incident response

00:03:07.735 --> 00:03:11.715
status, Mattermost Boards
provides end to end visibility.

00:03:12.295 --> 00:03:15.415
Staff can drag and drop
task cards between columns,

00:03:15.415 --> 00:03:18.055
update statuses,
and configure views,

00:03:18.055 --> 00:03:20.695
whether in a Kanban
board or table view,

00:03:20.695 --> 00:03:22.675
to accommodate the workflow.

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:30.400
With the threat contained,
the playbook run is closed.

00:03:32.100 --> 00:03:36.035
Built in reporting provides a timeline
and analysis for retrospective

00:03:43.355 --> 00:03:46.475
Mattermost aligns with
modern Zero Trust strategies.

00:03:46.475 --> 00:03:49.750
It enforces strict controls
with granular permissions and

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:51.350
supports SAML, LDAP,

00:03:51.350 --> 00:03:55.330
and multi factor authentication
for identity and access management.

00:03:55.350 --> 00:03:58.550
Segmentation is achieved with
teams and private channels.

00:03:58.550 --> 00:04:02.575
And data is protected with TLS
encryption and the ability to

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:05.995
enforce data retention
policies tailored for SecOps.

00:04:06.655 --> 00:04:09.935
Mattermost is the future of
cyber defense collaboration.

00:04:09.935 --> 00:04:12.655
Connect with us to explore how
Mattermost can transform your

00:04:12.655 --> 00:04:14.795
security workflows today.
